# {{TITLE}}

{{DESCRIPTION}}

[![CI](https://github.com/{{ORG}}/{{REPO}}/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg?branch=main)](https://github.com/{{ORG}}/{{REPO}}/actions/workflows/ci.yml)

An open board from [Kokeb Labs](https://github.com/kokeb-labs), built around the Kokeb Labs drivers.

> **Status: concept.** Nothing here has been built or verified on hardware. The status, revision and the drivers
> this board uses are in [`board.yml`](board.yml); read it before you rely on anything in this repository.

**Intended use.** Evaluation and development kit for electronics and firmware engineers. It is a component supplied
to people who build their own products. It is not a medical device and is not intended for diagnostic, therapeutic
or patient-connected use.

## What is here

| Path | What it holds |
| --- | --- |
| [`board.yml`](board.yml) | The board in one file: status, revision, intended use, drivers, variants, licences |
| [`trace/`](trace/SCHEMA.md) | Needs, requirements, risks and verifications, linked by version |
| [`hardware/`](hardware/README.md) | The KiCad project and reviews |
| [`mechanical/`](mechanical/README.md) | Enclosure and mounting |
| [`firmware/`](firmware/README.md) | Example firmware using the drivers |
| [`manufacturing/`](manufacturing/README.md) | The release package and checklist |
| [`verification/`](verification/README.md) | Test procedures and results |
| [`docs/`](docs/index.md) | Documentation, decisions and the [evidence pack](docs/evidence-pack.md) outline |

## Checks

```bash
python3 tools/kb_check.py --report build    # trace check and coverage report
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests       # tests of the check
```

CI runs both, with Markdown and YAML lint and the DCO sign-off check; the one required check is `CI gate / gate`.

## Contributing and support

Read the organisation's [contributing guide](https://github.com/kokeb-labs-open-boards/.github/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).
Questions and ideas go to [Discussions](https://github.com/orgs/kokeb-labs-open-boards/discussions); report a
vulnerability privately as the
[security policy](https://github.com/kokeb-labs-open-boards/.github/blob/main/SECURITY.md) describes.

